5-75 265 28C285 96 294 159 294 250C294 461 228 622 114 726L86 750L74 750C66 750 62 749 60 749Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-TEX-I-1D450\" d=\"M406 121C403 121 400 118 394 111C355 66 302 37 240 28C232 27 220 26 209 26C177 26 162 34 147 50C129 66 121 87 121 119C121 139 125 164 132 194C153 283 171 324 206 359C220 373 233 383 249 390C270 401 283 404 306 404C350 404 367 390 367 387L366 386C365 386 360 384 355 381C333 371 319 348 319 325C319 300 335 285 360 285C399 285 427 314 427 355C427 387 406 416 371 431C352 438 329 442 306 442C300 442 293 442 287 441C188 430 92 353 53 253C40 220 34 191 34 159C34 126 40 102 53 77C78 25 129-11 202-11C215-11 230-10 241-9C302 0 356 23 398 61C409 71 429 91 429 98C429 103 412 121 406 121Z\"></path></defs></svg>","mathFallback":false,"description":"JEE Advanced's 2019 JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Paper's All Questions with solutions provider ExamSIDE.Com","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline","nextq":"A8g0p6witsWypgXMEh1kjbpkjk7","questions":[{"question_id":"RcTHQyZZJCQQlmQdqq1kjboplbt","chapter":"aldehydes-ketones-and-carboxylic-acids","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-advanced","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":3,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline","permalink":"the-correct-order-of-acid-strength-of-the-following-carboxyl-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-40kdbo6pnxndzomr","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"The correct order of acid strength of the following carboxylic acids is\n<br><br><picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksrxwle2/f743808e-ad75-484e-b1cf-d3e74e144fb3/a423c1b0-05e1-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksrxwle3-320w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 500px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksrxwle2/f743808e-ad75-484e-b1cf-d3e74e144fb3/a423c1b0-05e1-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksrxwle3-500w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 680px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksrxwle2/f743808e-ad75-484e-b1cf-d3e74e144fb3/a423c1b0-05e1-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksrxwle3-680w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 860px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksrxwle2/f743808e-ad75-484e-b1cf-d3e74e144fb3/a423c1b0-05e1-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksrxwle3-860w.jpeg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksrxwle2/f743808e-ad75-484e-b1cf-d3e74e144fb3/a423c1b0-05e1-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksrxwle3.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 68 English\"></picture>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"III &gt; II &gt; I &gt; IV"},{"identifier":"B","content":"I &gt; II &gt; III &gt; IV"},{"identifier":"C","content":"II &gt; I &gt; IV &gt; III"},{"identifier":"D","content":"I &gt; III &gt; II &gt; IV"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"Acidic nature depends upon nature of electron withdrawing group and electronegativity. Electronegativity further depends on % of s character. Higher the s-character, greater will be the electronegativity and hence tendency to loose H increases thus acidic character also increases.<br><br> <img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksry43m6/ff82f8b9-0d19-4f4d-8db9-6d9db27d6454/74e1ddf0-05e2-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksry43m7.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 68 English Explanation 1\"> <br><br>sp- hybridisation (50% s character) (pK<sub>a</sub> = 1.86)<br><br> <img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksry4pni/cd8eda11-852e-4090-819d-4497a7d232fc/85e79fe0-05e2-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksry4pnj.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 68 English Explanation 2\"> <br><br>sp<sup>2</sup> - hybridisation (33-33% s character) (pK<sub>a</sub> = 4.3)<br><br> <picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksry5h8v/721841dc-4f61-47be-91d0-001edc849727/9b3851f0-05e2-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksry5h8w-320w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 500px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksry5h8v/721841dc-4f61-47be-91d0-001edc849727/9b3851f0-05e2-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksry5h8w-500w.jpeg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksry5h8v/721841dc-4f61-47be-91d0-001edc849727/9b3851f0-05e2-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksry5h8w.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 68 English Explanation 3\"></picture> <br><br>sp<sup>2</sup> - hybridisation (Resonance effect) (pK<sub>a</sub> = 4.5)<br><br> <img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksry5zl4/875e67d7-ce22-4b55-9228-8cb8ba468635/a9635590-05e2-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksry5zl5.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 68 English Explanation 4\"> <br><br>sp<sup>3</sup> - hybridisation (25% s-character) (pK<sub>a</sub> = 4.8)<br><br>Hence, acidic order I &gt; II &gt; III &gt; IV.<br><br>II is more acidic than III since electron donating group (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"8.074ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 3568.6 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1541,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2301,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is attached to benzene ring in III which decreases the acidic character.<br><br>On the other hand, pK<sub>a</sub> value also determined acidic nature, lower pK<sub>a</sub> value gives maximum acidic character.<br><br>Hence, option (b) is correct."},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>निम्न कार्बोक्सिलिक अम्लों की अम्ल प्रबलता का सही क्रम है</p>\n<p><picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksrxwle2/f743808e-ad75-484e-b1cf-d3e74e144fb3/a423c1b0-05e1-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksrxwle3-320w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 500px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksrxwle2/f743808e-ad75-484e-b1cf-d3e74e144fb3/a423c1b0-05e1-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksrxwle3-500w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 680px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksrxwle2/f743808e-ad75-484e-b1cf-d3e74e144fb3/a423c1b0-05e1-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksrxwle3-680w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 860px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksrxwle2/f743808e-ad75-484e-b1cf-d3e74e144fb3/a423c1b0-05e1-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksrxwle3-860w.jpeg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksrxwle2/f743808e-ad75-484e-b1cf-d3e74e144fb3/a423c1b0-05e1-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksrxwle3.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 68 Hindi\"></picture></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"III &gt; II &gt; I &gt; IV"},{"identifier":"B","content":"I &gt; II &gt; III &gt; IV"},{"identifier":"C","content":"II &gt; I &gt; IV &gt; III"},{"identifier":"D","content":"I &gt; III &gt; II &gt; IV"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"अम्लीय प्रकृति इलेक्ट्रॉन आकर्षित करने वाले समूह की प्रकृति और विद्युत ऋणात्मकता पर निर्भर करती है। विद्युत ऋणात्मकता आगे s संकेत के % पर निर्भर करती है। s-संकेत जितना अधिक होगा, विद्युत ऋणात्मकता उतनी ही अधिक होगी और इसलिए H को मुक्त करने की प्रवृत्ति बढ़ती है इस प्रकार अम्लीय गुण भी बढ़ता है।<br><br> <img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksry43m6/ff82f8b9-0d19-4f4d-8db9-6d9db27d6454/74e1ddf0-05e2-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksry43m7.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 68 Hindi Explanation 1\"> <br><br>sp- संकरण (50% s संकेत) (pK<sub>a</sub> = 1.86)<br><br> <img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksry4pni/cd8eda11-852e-4090-819d-4497a7d232fc/85e79fe0-05e2-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksry4pnj.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 68 Hindi Explanation 2\"> <br><br>sp<sup>2</sup> - संकरण (33-33% s संकेत) (pK<sub>a</sub> = 4.3)<br><br> <picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksry5h8v/721841dc-4f61-47be-91d0-001edc849727/9b3851f0-05e2-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksry5h8w-320w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 500px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksry5h8v/721841dc-4f61-47be-91d0-001edc849727/9b3851f0-05e2-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksry5h8w-500w.jpeg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksry5h8v/721841dc-4f61-47be-91d0-001edc849727/9b3851f0-05e2-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksry5h8w.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 68 Hindi Explanation 3\"></picture> <br><br>sp<sup>2</sup> - संकरण (अनुनाद प्रभाव) (pK<sub>a</sub> = 4.5)<br><br> <img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksry5zl4/875e67d7-ce22-4b55-9228-8cb8ba468635/a9635590-05e2-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksry5zl5.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 68 Hindi Explanation 4\"> <br><br>sp<sup>3</sup> - संकरण (25% s-संकेत) (pK<sub>a</sub> = 4.8)<br><br>अतः, अम्लीय क्रम I &gt; II &gt; III &gt; IV है।<br><br>II, III की तुलना में अधिक अम्लीय है क्योंकि III में बेंजीन वलय से इलेक्ट्रॉन दाता समूह (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"8.074ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 3568.6 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1541,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2301,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) जुड़ा हुआ है जो अम्लीय गुण को कम करता है।<br><br>दूसरी ओर, pK<sub>a</sub> मान भी अम्लीय प्रकृति निर्धारित करता है, निम्न pK<sub>a</sub> मान अधिकतम अम्लीय गुण देता है।<br><br>अतः, विकल्प (b) सही है।"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":200000,"topic":"preparation-properties-and-uses-of-carboxylic-acids","type":"mcq","year":2019,"paperId":"jee-advanced-2019-paper-1-offline","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"jee-advanced-2019-paper-1-offline","active":true},{"question_id":"hCDDyE57KWgkhZFWSS1kjbow9qk","chapter":"d-and-f-block-elements","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-advanced","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":3,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline","permalink":"the-green-colour-produced-in-the-borax-bead-test-of-a-chromi-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-mtdave5mpefdxjrs","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"The green colour produced in the borax bead test of a chromium (III) salt is due to ","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Cr<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"CrB"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Cr(BO<sub>2</sub>)<sub>3</sub>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Cr<sub>2</sub>(B<sub>4</sub>O<sub>7</sub>)<sub>3</sub>"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"Borax bead test is performed only for coloured salt. Borax (sodium pyroborate), Na<sub>2</sub>B<sub>4</sub>O<sub>7</sub>.10H<sub>2</sub>O on heating gets fused and lose water of crystallisation. It swells up into fluffy white porous mass which melts into a colourless liquid which later form a clear transparent glassy bead consisting of boric anhydride and sodium metaborate.<br><br> <picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksus9wsj/fd352163-777e-4fc8-be03-b6826eda089f/f9a39930-0771-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksus9wsk-320w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 500px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksus9wsj/fd352163-777e-4fc8-be03-b6826eda089f/f9a39930-0771-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksus9wsk-500w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 680px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksus9wsj/fd352163-777e-4fc8-be03-b6826eda089f/f9a39930-0771-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksus9wsk-680w.jpeg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksus9wsj/fd352163-777e-4fc8-be03-b6826eda089f/f9a39930-0771-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksus9wsk.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - d and f Block Elements Question 20 English Explanation 1\"></picture> <br><br>Boric anhydride is non-volatile. When it react with Cr(III) salt then deep green complex is formed.<br><br> <picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksusak32/a8d7592d-011e-48f1-aa9c-68e54ff0b1ea/0ba1ebf0-0772-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksusak33-320w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 500px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksusak32/a8d7592d-011e-48f1-aa9c-68e54ff0b1ea/0ba1ebf0-0772-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksusak33-500w.jpeg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksusak32/a8d7592d-011e-48f1-aa9c-68e54ff0b1ea/0ba1ebf0-0772-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksusak33.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - d and f Block Elements Question 20 English Explanation 2\"></picture> <br><br>Hence, option (c) is correct."},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>क्रोमियम(III) लवण के सुहागा-मनका परीक्षण (borax bead test) में हरे रंग का कारण है</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Cr<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"CrB"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Cr(BO<sub>2</sub>)<sub>3</sub>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Cr<sub>2</sub>(B<sub>4</sub>O<sub>7</sub>)<sub>3</sub>"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"बोरेक्स मणिका परीक्षण केवल रंगीन लवणों के लिए किया जाता है। बोरेक्स (सोडियम पाइरोबोरेट), Na<sub>2</sub>B<sub>4</sub>O<sub>7</sub>.10H<sub>2</sub>O को गर्म करने पर यह संगलित हो जाता है और क्रिस्टलीकरण का जल खो देता है। यह एक फूले हुए सफेद झरझरे द्रव्यमान में फैल जाता है जो एक रंगहीन द्रव में पिघल जाता है जो बाद में एक स्पष्ट पारदर्शी कांच जैसी मणिका बनाता है जिसमें बोरिक एनहाइड्राइड और सोडियम मेटाबोरेट होते हैं।<br><br> <picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksus9wsj/fd352163-777e-4fc8-be03-b6826eda089f/f9a39930-0771-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksus9wsk-320w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 500px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksus9wsj/fd352163-777e-4fc8-be03-b6826eda089f/f9a39930-0771-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksus9wsk-500w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 680px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksus9wsj/fd352163-777e-4fc8-be03-b6826eda089f/f9a39930-0771-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksus9wsk-680w.jpeg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksus9wsj/fd352163-777e-4fc8-be03-b6826eda089f/f9a39930-0771-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksus9wsk.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - d and f Block Elements Question 20 Hindi Explanation 1\"></picture> <br><br>बोरिक एनहाइड्राइड अवाष्पशील है। जब यह Cr(III) लवण के साथ अभिक्रिया करता है तो गहरा हरा संकुल बनता है।<br><br> <picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksusak32/a8d7592d-011e-48f1-aa9c-68e54ff0b1ea/0ba1ebf0-0772-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksusak33-320w.jpeg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 500px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksusak32/a8d7592d-011e-48f1-aa9c-68e54ff0b1ea/0ba1ebf0-0772-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksusak33-500w.jpeg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksusak32/a8d7592d-011e-48f1-aa9c-68e54ff0b1ea/0ba1ebf0-0772-11ec-a0ab-05c984536117/file-1ksusak33.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - d and f Block Elements Question 20 Hindi Explanation 2\"></picture> <br><br>अतः, विकल्प (c) सही है।"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":200000,"topic":"important-compounds-of-transition-elements","type":"mcq","year":2019,"paperId":"jee-advanced-2019-paper-1-offline","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"jee-advanced-2019-paper-1-offline","active":true},{"question_id":"M837OE8hyx7RB6n9oJ1kjbp3n2g","chapter":"isolation-of-elements","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-advanced","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":3,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline","permalink":"calamine-malachite-magnetic-and-cryolite-respectively-ar-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-owme91fiavz71s0s","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"Calamine, malachite, magnetic and cryolite, respectively, are","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"ZnCO<sub>3</sub>, CuCO<sub>3</sub>, Fe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>, Na<sub>3</sub>AlF<sub>6</sub>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"ZnSO<sub>4</sub>, CuCO<sub>3</sub>, Fe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>, AlF<sub>3</sub>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"ZnSO<sub>4</sub>, Cu(OH)<sub>2</sub>, Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub>, Na<sub>3</sub>AlF<sub>6</sub>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"ZnCO<sub>3</sub>, CuCO<sub>3</sub>.Cu(OH)<sub>2</sub>, Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub>, Na<sub>3</sub>AlF<sub>6</sub>"}],"correct_options":["D"],"answer":null,"explanation":"ZnCO<sub>3</sub> - Calamine (zinc ore)<br><br>CuCO<sub>3</sub>.Cu(OH)<sub>2</sub> - Malachite (copper ore)<br><br>Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> - Magnetite (iron ore)<br><br>Na<sub>3</sub>AlF<sub>6</sub> - Cryolite (aluminum ore)<br><br>Thus, option (d) is correct.\n<br><br><b>Note : ( Remember all those ores names. Any one of those can be asked in the exam.)</b>\n<br><br><b>Oxides Ores :</b>\n<br><br> (1) ZnO - Zincite<br><br>(2) Fe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> - Haematite<br><br>(3) Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> - Magnetite (FeO + Fe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> mixture)<br><br>(4) Fe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> . 3H<sub>2</sub>O - Limonite<br><br>(5) MnO<sub>2</sub> - Pyrolusite<br><br>(6) Cu<sub>2</sub>O - Cuprite or Ruby Copper<br><br>(7) TiO<sub>2</sub> - Rutile<br><br>(8) FeCr<sub>2</sub>O<sub>4</sub> - Chromite (FeO + Cr<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>)<br><br>(9) FeTiO<sub>3</sub> - Illmenite (FeO + TiO<sub>2</sub>)<br><br>(10) Na<sub>2</sub>B<sub>4</sub>O<sub>7</sub> . 10H<sub>2</sub>O - Borax or Tincal<br><br>(11) U<sub>3</sub>O<sub>8</sub> - Pitch Blende<br><br>(12) SnO<sub>2</sub> - Tin Stone or Cassiterite<br><br>(13) Ca<sub>2</sub>B<sub>6</sub>O<sub>11</sub> . 5H<sub>2</sub>O - Colemanite (2 Cao + 3 B<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>)<br><br>(14) Al<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> . 2H<sub>2</sub>O - Bauxite<br><br>(15) Al<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> . H<sub>2</sub>O - Diaspore<br><br>(16) Al<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> - Corundum\n<br><br><b>Sulphides Ores :</b>\n<br><br>(1) ZnS - Zinc Blende or Sphalerite<br><br>(2) PbS - Galena<br><br>(3) Ag<sub>2</sub>S - Argentite or Silver Glance<br><br>(4) HgS - Cinnabar<br><br>(5) Cu<sub>2</sub>S - Chalcocite or Copper glance<br><br>(6) CuFeS<sub>2</sub> - Copper pyrites or Chalco pyrites (Cu<sub>2</sub>S + Fe<sub>2</sub>S<sub>3</sub> mixture)<br><br>(7) FeS<sub>2</sub> - Iron pyrites or Fool's Gold<br><br>(8) 3Ag<sub>2</sub>S . Sb<sub>2</sub>S<sub>2</sub> - Pyrargyrite or ruby silver\n<br><br> <b>Halides Ores :</b><br><br>(1) NaCl - Rock Salt<br><br>(2) KCl - Sylvine<br><br>(3) Na<sub>3</sub>AlF<sub>6</sub> - Cryolite [3NaF + AlF<sub>6</sub>]<br><br>(4) CaF<sub>2</sub> - Fluorspar<br><br>(5) KCl . MgCl<sub>2</sub> . 6H<sub>2</sub>O - Carnalite<br><br>(6) AgCl - Horn Silver\n<br><br><b>Carbonates Ores :</b><br><br>(1) CaCO<sub>3</sub> - Limestone<br><br>(2) MgCO<sub>3</sub> - Magnesite<br><br>(3) CaCO<sub>3</sub> . MgCO<sub>3</sub> - Dolomite<br><br>(4) ZnCO<sub>3</sub> - Calamine<br><br>(5) PbCO<sub>3</sub> - Cerrusite<br><br>(6) FeCO<sub>3</sub> - Siderite<br><br>(7) CuCO<sub>3</sub> . Cu(OH)<sub>2</sub> or Cu<sub>2</sub>CO<sub>3</sub>(OH)<sub>2</sub> - Malachite or Basic Copper Carbonates<br><br>(8) 2 CuCO<sub>3</sub> . Cu(OH)<sub>2</sub> - Azurite\n<br><br><b>Sulphates Ores :</b><br><br>(1) CuSO<sub>4</sub> . 2H<sub>2</sub>O - Gypsum<br><br>(2) MgSO<sub>4</sub> . 7H<sub>2</sub>O - Epson Salt<br><br>(3) Na<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub> . 10 H<sub>2</sub>O - Glauber's Salt<br><br>(4) PbSO<sub>4</sub> - Anglesite<br><br>(5) ZnSO<sub>4</sub> . 7H<sub>2</sub>O - White Vitriol<br><br>(6) FeSO<sub>4</sub> . 7H<sub>2</sub>O - Green Vitriol<br><br>(7) CuSO<sub>4</sub> . 5H<sub>2</sub>O - Blue Vitriol or Chalcanthite<br><br><b>Nitrate Ores :</b><br><br>(1) KNO<sub>3</sub> - Indian Saltpetre<br><br>(2) NaNO<sub>3</sub> - Chile Saltpetre<br><br><b>Arsenides Ores :</b><br><br>(1) NiAs - Kupfernickel<br><br>(2) NiAsS - Nickel glance"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>कैलामीन (calamine), मैलाकाइट (malachite), मैग्रेटाइट (magnetite) और क्रायोलाइट (cryolite) क्रमशः हैं</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"ZnCO<sub>3</sub>, CuCO<sub>3</sub>, Fe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>, Na<sub>3</sub>AlF<sub>6</sub>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"ZnSO<sub>4</sub>, CuCO<sub>3</sub>, Fe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>, AlF<sub>3</sub>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"ZnSO<sub>4</sub>, Cu(OH)<sub>2</sub>, Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub>, Na<sub>3</sub>AlF<sub>6</sub>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"ZnCO<sub>3</sub>, CuCO<sub>3</sub>.Cu(OH)<sub>2</sub>, Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub>, Na<sub>3</sub>AlF<sub>6</sub>"}],"correct_options":["D"],"answer":null,"explanation":"ZnCO<sub>3</sub> - कैलामाइन (जिंक अयस्क)<br><br>CuCO<sub>3</sub>.Cu(OH)<sub>2</sub> - मैलाकाइट (कॉपर अयस्क)<br><br>Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> - मैग्नेटाइट (लौह अयस्क)<br><br>Na<sub>3</sub>AlF<sub>6</sub> - क्रायोलाइट (एल्युमिनियम अयस्क)<br><br>इस प्रकार, विकल्प (d) सही है।\n<br><br><b>नोट : (इन सभी अयस्कों के नाम याद रखें। परीक्षा में इनमें से कोई भी पूछा जा सकता है।)</b>\n<br><br><b>ऑक्साइड अयस्क :</b>\n<br><br> (1) ZnO - जिंकाइट<br><br>(2) Fe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> - हेमेटाइट<br><br>(3) Fe<sub>3</sub>O<sub>4</sub> - मैग्नेटाइट (FeO + Fe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> मिश्रण)<br><br>(4) Fe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> . 3H<sub>2</sub>O - लिमोनाइट<br><br>(5) MnO<sub>2</sub> - पाइरोलुसाइट<br><br>(6) Cu<sub>2</sub>O - क्यूप्राइट या रूबी कॉपर<br><br>(7) TiO<sub>2</sub> - रुटाइल<br><br>(8) FeCr<sub>2</sub>O<sub>4</sub> - क्रोमाइट (FeO + Cr<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>)<br><br>(9) FeTiO<sub>3</sub> - इल्मेनाइट (FeO + TiO<sub>2</sub>)<br><br>(10) Na<sub>2</sub>B<sub>4</sub>O<sub>7</sub> . 10H<sub>2</sub>O - बोरेक्स या टिंकल<br><br>(11) U<sub>3</sub>O<sub>8</sub> - पिच ब्लेंड<br><br>(12) SnO<sub>2</sub> - टिन स्टोन या कैसिटेराइट<br><br>(13) Ca<sub>2</sub>B<sub>6</sub>O<sub>11</sub> . 5H<sub>2</sub>O - कोलेमेनाइट (2 Cao + 3 B<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>)<br><br>(14) Al<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> . 2H<sub>2</sub>O - बॉक्साइट<br><br>(15) Al<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> . H<sub>2</sub>O - डायस्पोर<br><br>(16) Al<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> - कोरंडम\n<br><br><b>सल्फाइड अयस्क :</b>\n<br><br>(1) ZnS - जिंक ब्लेंड या स्फालेराइट<br><br>(2) PbS - गैलेना<br><br>(3) Ag<sub>2</sub>S - अर्जेंटाइट या सिल्वर ग्लांस<br><br>(4) HgS - सिनेबार<br><br>(5) Cu<sub>2</sub>S - कैल्कोसाइट या कॉपर ���्लांस<br><br>(6) CuFeS<sub>2</sub> - कॉपर पाइराइट्स या कैल्को पाइराइट्स (Cu<sub>2</sub>S + Fe<sub>2</sub>S<sub>3</sub> मिश्रण)<br><br>(7) FeS<sub>2</sub> - आयरन पाइराइट्स या फूल्स गोल्ड<br><br>(8) 3Ag<sub>2</sub>S . Sb<sub>2</sub>S<sub>2</sub> - पाइरार्जिराइट या रूबी सिल्वर\n<br><br> <b>हैलाइड अयस्क :</b><br><br>(1) NaCl - रॉक साल्ट<br><br>(2) KCl - सिल्वाइन<br><br>(3) Na<sub>3</sub>AlF<sub>6</sub> - क्रायोलाइट [3NaF + AlF<sub>6</sub>]<br><br>(4) CaF<sub>2</sub> - फ्लोरस्पार<br><br>(5) KCl . MgCl<sub>2</sub> . 6H<sub>2</sub>O - कार्नेलाइट<br><br>(6) AgCl - हॉर्न सिल्वर\n<br><br><b>कार्बोनेट अयस्क :</b><br><br>(1) CaCO<sub>3</sub> - लाइमस्टोन<br><br>(2) MgCO<sub>3</sub> - मैग्नेसाइट<br><br>(3) CaCO<sub>3</sub> . MgCO<sub>3</sub> - डोलोमाइट<br><br>(4) ZnCO<sub>3</sub> - कैलामाइन<br><br>(5) PbCO<sub>3</sub> - सेरुसाइट<br><br>(6) FeCO<sub>3</sub> - सिडेराइट<br><br>(7) CuCO<sub>3</sub> . Cu(OH)<sub>2</sub> या Cu<sub>2</sub>CO<sub>3</sub>(OH)<sub>2</sub> - मैलाकाइट या बेसिक कॉपर कार्बोनेट<br><br>(8) 2 CuCO<sub>3</sub> . Cu(OH)<sub>2</sub> - एज़्यूराइट\n<br><br><b>सल्फेट अयस्क :</b><br><br>(1) CuSO<sub>4</sub> . 2H<sub>2</sub>O - जिप्सम<br><br>(2) MgSO<sub>4</sub> . 7H<sub>2</sub>O - एप्सम साल्ट<br><br>(3) Na<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub> . 10 H<sub>2</sub>O - ग्लॉबर साल्ट<br><br>(4) PbSO<sub>4</sub> - एंग्लेसाइट<br><br>(5) ZnSO<sub>4</sub> . 7H<sub>2</sub>O - व्हाइट विट्रियल<br><br>(6) FeSO<sub>4</sub> . 7H<sub>2</sub>O - ग्रीन विट्रियल<br><br>(7) CuSO<sub>4</sub> . 5H<sub>2</sub>O - ब्लू विट्रियल या कैल्कैन्थाइट<br><br><b>नाइट्रेट अयस्क :</b><br><br>(1) KNO<sub>3</sub> - इंडियन साल्टपीटर<br><br>(2) NaNO<sub>3</sub> - चिली साल्टपीटर<br><br><b>आर्सेनाइड अयस्क :</b><br><br>(1) NiAs - कुफरनिकेल<br><br>(2) NiAsS - निकेल ग्लांस"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":200000,"topic":"minerals-and-ores","type":"mcq","year":2019,"paperId":"jee-advanced-2019-paper-1-offline","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"jee-advanced-2019-paper-1-offline","active":true},{"question_id":"s80pl0WGObJd1ccV8h1kjbpb9tu","chapter":"electrochemistry","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-advanced","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":3,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline","permalink":"molar-conductivity-lambda-submsub-of-aqueous-sol-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-aqzr3iqtrolmtea7","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"Molar conductivity (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.57ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 694 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"39B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-39B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><sub>m</sub>) of aqueous solution of sodium stearate, which behaves as a strong electrolyte, is recorded at varying concentrations (C) of sodium stearate. Which one of the following plots provides the correct representation of micelle formation in the solution?<br><br>(critical micelle concentration (CMC) is marked with an arrow in the figures)","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksry9z2o/3cf6e7a8-bad1-4bbb-96bf-25e053f37407/183a6d00-05e3-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksry9z2p.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Electrochemistry Question 26 English Option 1\">"},{"identifier":"B","content":"<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksryaa2e/5009672f-b8d1-49c7-9f14-058edf9ea6a4/20b83160-05e3-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksryaa2f.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Electrochemistry Question 26 English Option 2\">"},{"identifier":"C","content":"<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksryap25/10d9e8e5-cc47-42ce-b7e2-b5310589a664/2c4d20d0-05e3-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksryap26.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Electrochemistry Question 26 English Option 3\">"},{"identifier":"D","content":"<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksryb3i7/ec57d2a1-13c3-491d-94db-e0d68df6eb1a/3775e0f0-05e3-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksryb3i8.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Electrochemistry Question 26 English Option 4\">"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"At normal or low concentration, sodium stearate (CH<sub>3</sub>(CH<sub>2</sub>)<sub>16</sub>COO<sup>-</sup>Na<sup>+</sup>] behaves as strong electrolyte and for strong electrolyte, molar conductance (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.57ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 694 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"39B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-39B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><sub>m</sub>) decreases with increase in concentration. Above particular concentration, sodium stearate forms aggregates known as micelles. The concentration is called as CMC. Since, number of ions decreases and hence <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.57ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 694 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"39B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-39B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><sub>m</sub> also decreases.<br><br>Hence, option (c) is correct."},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>सोडियम स्टिऐरेट (sodium stearate) के जलीय विलयन, जो एक प्रबल विद्युतअपघटय (electrolyte) जैसा व्यवहार दर्शाता है, की मोलर चालकता <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.923ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 2175.8 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(389,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"39B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-39B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(727,-150) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45A\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1786.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> को विभित्र सान्द्रताओं <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.74ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 1211 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(389,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D450\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D450\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(822,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> मे मापा गया । निम्न चित्रों में से मिसेल विरचन (micelle formation) दर्शाने वाला सही चित्र कौन सा है ? (क्रांतिक मिसेल सान्द्रता (critical micelle concentration, CMC) को चित्रों में तीर द्वारा दर्शाया गया है)</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksry9z2o/3cf6e7a8-bad1-4bbb-96bf-25e053f37407/183a6d00-05e3-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksry9z2p.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Electrochemistry Question 26 Hindi Option 1\">"},{"identifier":"B","content":"<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksryaa2e/5009672f-b8d1-49c7-9f14-058edf9ea6a4/20b83160-05e3-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksryaa2f.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Electrochemistry Question 26 Hindi Option 2\">"},{"identifier":"C","content":"<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksryap25/10d9e8e5-cc47-42ce-b7e2-b5310589a664/2c4d20d0-05e3-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksryap26.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Electrochemistry Question 26 Hindi Option 3\">"},{"identifier":"D","content":"<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ksryb3i7/ec57d2a1-13c3-491d-94db-e0d68df6eb1a/3775e0f0-05e3-11ec-aff4-f93815541f69/file-1ksryb3i8.jpeg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Electrochemistry Question 26 Hindi Option 4\">"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"सामान्य या निम्न सांद्रता पर, सोडियम स्टीयरेट (CH<sub>3</sub>(CH<sub>2</sub>)<sub>16</sub>COO<sup>-</sup>Na<sup>+</sup>] प्रबल विद्युत-अपघट्य की तरह व्यवहार करता है और प्रबल विद्युत-अपघट्य के लिए, मोलर चालकता (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.57ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 694 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"39B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-39B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><sub>m</sub>) सांद्रता में वृद्धि के साथ घटती है। एक विशेष सांद्रता से अधिक होने पर, सोडियम स्टीयरेट समुच्चय बनाता है जिन्हें मिसेल कहते हैं। इस सांद्रता को CMC कहा जाता है। चूँकि, आयनों की संख्या घटती है और इसलिए <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.57ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 694 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"39B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-39B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><sub>m</sub> भी घटता है।<br><br>अतः, विकल्प (c) सही है।"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":200000,"topic":"conductance-and-electrolysis","type":"mcq","year":2019,"paperId":"jee-advanced-2019-paper-1-offline","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"jee-advanced-2019-paper-1-offline","active":true}],"ids":["RcTHQyZZJCQQlmQdqq1kjboplbt","hCDDyE57KWgkhZFWSS1kjbow9qk","M837OE8hyx7RB6n9oJ1kjbp3n2g","s80pl0WGObJd1ccV8h1kjbpb9tu"],"title":"JEE Advanced 2019 Paper 1 Offline | JEE Advanced Year Wise Previous Years Questions","canonical":"https://app/past-years/jee/the-correct-order-of-acid-strength-of-the-following-carboxyl-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-40kdbo6p